DevOps vs MLOps

| DevOps                      | MLOps                              |
| --------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |
| Software applications       | Machine-learning applications      |
| Code                        | Code + Data + Model                |
| Build & test software       | Train & evaluate models            |
| Deploy application          | Deploy ML model                    |
| Monitor application         | Monitor model + predictions + data |
| CI/CD                       | CI/CT/CD                           |
| Docker, Jenkins, Kubernetes | SageMaker, MLflow, Kubeflow, etc.  |


=====

Your SageMaker project

For your insurance prediction project, you're doing MLOps when you:

Dataset
   ↓
Train Random Forest
   ↓
Save model (.joblib)
   ↓
Upload model to S3
   ↓
Create SageMaker Model
   ↓
Create Endpoint
   ↓
Make predictions
   ↓
Monitor
   ↓
Retrain/update model

And you're using DevOps concepts when you automate the surrounding software deployment—for example, GitHub → testing → Docker → AWS deployment.

Simple way to remember:

DevOps manages software in production.
MLOps manages ML models and the entire ML lifecycle in production.

